<div class="api-symbol-body">

Remove default button style animations

<p class="api-slot-label">Returns</p>

- <code class="api-type">druid_button</code> — The current button instance

</div>

#### \`druid_button.set_enabled(state?: boolean | undefined): druid_button\`

<div class="api-symbol-body">

Set button enabled state.
The style.on_set_enabled will be triggered.
Disabled button is not clickable.

<p class="api-slot-label">Parameters</p>

- <strong class="api-name">\`state\`</strong>?: <code class="api-type">boolean | undefined</code> — Enabled state

<p class="api-slot-label">Returns</p>

- <code class="api-type">druid_button</code> — The current button instance

</div>

#### \`druid_button.is_enabled(): boolean\`

<div class="api-symbol-body">

Get button enabled state.
By default all Buttons are enabled on creating.

<p class="api-slot-label">Returns</p>

- <code class="api-type">boolean</code> — True, if button is enabled now, False otherwise

</div>

#### \`druid_button.set_click_zone(zone?: Opaque<"node"> | string | undefined): druid_button\`

<div class="api-symbol-body">

Set additional button click area.
Useful to restrict click outside of stencil node or scrollable content.
If button node placed inside stencil node, it will be automatically set to this stencil node.

<p class="api-slot-label">Parameters</p>

- <strong class="api-name">\`zone\`</strong>?: <code class="api-type">Opaque&lt;&quot;node&quot;&gt; | string | undefined</code> — Gui node

<p class="api-slot-label">Returns</p>

- <code class="api-type">druid_button</code> — The current button instance

</div>

#### \`druid_button.set_key_trigger(key: Hash | string): druid_button\`

<div class="api-symbol-body">

Set key name to trigger this button by keyboard.

<p class="api-slot-label">Parameters</p>

- <strong class="api-name">\`key\`</strong>: <code class="api-type">Hash | string</code> — The action_id of the input key. Example: "key_space"

<p class="api-slot-label">Returns</p>

- <code class="api-type">druid_button</code> — The current button instance

</div>

#### \`druid_button.get_key_trigger(): Hash\`

<div class="api-symbol-body">

Get current key name to trigger this button.

<p class="api-slot-label">Returns</p>

- <code class="api-type">Hash</code> — The action_id of the input key

</div>

#### \`druid_button.set_check_function(check_function?: ((...args: any[]) => unknown) | undefined, failure_callback?: ((...args: any[]) => unknown) | undefined): druid_button\`

<div class="api-symbol-body">

Set function for additional check for button click availability.

<p class="api-slot-label">Parameters</p>

- <strong class="api-name">\`check_function\`</strong>?: <code class="api-type">((...args: any[]) =&gt; unknown) | undefined</code> — Should return true or false. If true - button can be pressed.
- <strong class="api-name">\`failure_callback\`</strong>?: <code class="api-type">((...args: any[]) =&gt; unknown) | undefined</code> — Function will be called on button click, if check function returns false

<p class="api-slot-label">Returns</p>

- <code class="api-type">druid_button</code> — The current button instance

</div>

#### \`druid_button.set_web_user_interaction(is_web_mode?: boolean | undefined): druid_button\`

<div class="api-symbol-body">

Set Button mode to work inside user HTML5 interaction event.

It's required to make protected things like copy & paste text, show mobile keyboard, etc
The HTML5 button doesn't call any events except on_click event.

If the game is not HTML, html mode will be not enabled

<p class="api-slot-label">Parameters</p>

- <strong class="api-name">\`is_web_mode\`</strong>?: <code class="api-type">boolean | undefined</code> — If true - button will be called inside html5 callback

<p class="api-slot-label">Returns</p>

- <code class="api-type">druid_button</code> — The current button instance

</div>

